1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,850
Hello, this is Liam, in for Bear.

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:05,536
Medhavy Hub is the front door to a fleet
of protected textbooks.

3
00:00:05,586 --> 00:00:09,221
One sign-in, one set of roles, one place
to approve who gets in.

4
00:00:09,271 --> 00:00:11,813
This is a suggested prompt, not a
transcript.

5
00:00:11,863 --> 00:00:16,700
The footage is the live admin, driven by a
scripted browser, with every name masked.

6
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:20,896
The hub does not hand your students a
password for each book. They sign in once.

7
00:00:20,946 --> 00:00:25,353
For every textbook they are entitled to,
the hub mints a twenty-four-hour token,
and

8
00:00:25,403 --> 00:00:27,954
the textbook site checks it back against
the hub.

9
00:00:28,004 --> 00:00:31,719
Three roles: student, instructor, admin.
Today we walk the admin side.

10
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:37,005
The admin panel opens on the numbers:
seventy-nine users, eleven admins, no
pending

11
00:00:37,055 --> 00:00:39,698
requests. Below it, the textbook registry.

12
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:43,659
Each book has a URL and a status: public,
private, or hidden.

13
00:00:45,133 --> 00:00:47,932
View All lists every book with an Open
button.

14
00:00:47,982 --> 00:00:50,534
Clicking it mints the token and redirects.

15
00:00:50,584 --> 00:00:54,733
Source fact: registering a URL also
whitelists its origin for CORS.

16
00:00:56,133 --> 00:00:59,886
Users: the first hundred Clerk accounts,
names masked here.

17
00:00:59,936 --> 00:01:01,626
Each row has a role select.

18
00:01:01,676 --> 00:01:05,413
Admin rows are locked; the API refuses to
demote an admin.

19
00:01:07,133 --> 00:01:08,756
View Admins is the short list.

20
00:01:08,806 --> 00:01:13,441
Classes is where instructors live: two
live classes, eight and thirteen students,
an

21
00:01:13,491 --> 00:01:14,278
archive button.

22
00:01:14,328 --> 00:01:18,795
Students join a class with an invite code,
and enrollment is what grants textbook

23
00:01:18,845 --> 00:01:22,024
access. That is the mechanism, not a
separate permission.

24
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:30,953
Concept Maps: import a pipeline run by
timestamp, review every node by hand,
export

25
00:01:31,003 --> 00:01:36,336
a verified map. Four sessions here. Grant
Access lets an instructor into the editor.

26
00:01:36,733 --> 00:01:41,200
Requests is empty today. A student's ask
for a private book lands here.

27
00:01:41,250 --> 00:01:43,731
Approve or deny; their library updates.

28
00:01:44,033 --> 00:01:45,345
Analytics runs on PostHog.

29
00:01:45,395 --> 00:01:49,691
Eighty unique users in thirty days, four
hundred twenty-nine page views, thirty-six

30
00:01:49,741 --> 00:01:51,890
textbook opens, fifty-one AI interactions.

31
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:56,027
Platform breakdown shows the hub, then the
cancer textbook, then dev instances.

32
00:01:56,077 --> 00:01:59,274
The Students and Instructors views rank
engagement per person.

33
00:01:59,324 --> 00:02:03,358
Trade-off: the hub's own session counter
is a separate system, and its summary

34
00:02:03,408 --> 00:02:05,921
writes are not atomic. Rough stats, not
billing.

35
00:02:12,733 --> 00:02:15,172
Settings is Clerk's own profile card.

36
00:02:15,222 --> 00:02:18,451
The name lives here; the role lives in
metadata.

37
00:02:19,633 --> 00:02:23,736
Observed on the live admin: a registry
with three statuses, user roles with the

38
00:02:23,786 --> 00:02:27,837
admin lock, classes, concept-map sessions,
an empty request queue, and PostHog

39
00:02:27,887 --> 00:02:32,095
analytics. Not shown: the student library,
the request flow, and the invite join.

40
00:02:32,145 --> 00:02:35,565
Those need a second account. Also not
shown: the textbook handoff.

41
00:02:35,615 --> 00:02:39,508
All three textbook sites bounced back to
the hub with a localhost redirect.

42
00:02:39,558 --> 00:02:41,713
That is a bug to fix, not a demo to fake.

43
00:02:41,733 --> 00:02:45,392
Your turn. Read the creating-a-new-
textbook guide in the hub repo.

44
00:02:45,442 --> 00:02:49,325
Register one textbook as private, protect
its site, grant one student.

45
00:02:49,375 --> 00:02:52,753
Then sign in as that student and watch the
token do the work.

46
00:02:52,803 --> 00:02:56,005
One book, one student, one comparison.
Liam, in for Bear.

47
00:02:56,033 --> 00:03:00,321
Medhavy Hub: One Sign-In, Every Textbook.
At Nik Bear Brown.
